; A sliding puzzle on a board of two rows of three: the blank trades places
; with a neighbouring tile. Exploration visits each reachable board once, so
; the explored states are the 6!/2 = 360 boards of the start's parity; every
; board can move, so there is no outcome and the run is a cycle. On the 3x3
; board the same two rules visit 9!/2 = 181,440 boards.
(step one)
(at p1 t1) (at p2 t2) (at p3 t3) (at p4 t4) (at p5 t5) (at p6 blank)
(adj p1 p2) (adj p2 p3) (adj p4 p5) (adj p5 p6) (adj p1 p4) (adj p2 p5) (adj p3 p6)
(rule slide (take (at $p blank) (at $q $t)) (read (adj $p $q)) (make (at $p $t) (at $q blank)))
(rule slide-back (take (at $p blank) (at $q $t)) (read (adj $q $p)) (make (at $p $t) (at $q blank)))
